From db71d997793b5c91eab027b3cb6b2e87bf178270 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 20:20:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix Prisma/Neon adapter version mismatch
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

@prisma/adapter-neon was pinned to 7.10.0 (Prisma ORM v7's driver-adapter
API) while @prisma/client and prisma stayed on 5.22.0, an incompatible
pairing that crashed at runtime ("Cannot read properties of undefined
(reading 'bind')") the moment PrismaClient({ adapter }) actually ran —
masked until now by two @ts-expect-error comments suppressing the type
errors that would've flagged it. This surfaced during the Cloudflare
build because OpenNext's page-data collection step evaluates lib/db.ts
eagerly, but it was never actually Cloudflare-specific and would have
broken any real production build.

Fix: pin @prisma/adapter-neon to 5.22.0 and @neondatabase/serverless to
^0.10.4, the version pairing @prisma/adapter-neon@5.22.0 actually
supports, and drop the now-unnecessary @ts-expect-error comments.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PmGzXu2VBxGGDAmDZYhgdT
